 Erling Haaland, Jean-Philippe Mateta and Nick Woltemade all performed well but there was disappointment for Alexander Isak, Joao Pedro and Viktor Gyokeres.<br /><br />James, Mark and Sam discuss if it’s time to get rid of those underperforming strikers or if it’s worth holding onto them a little longer.<br /><br />They also chat about Nottingham Forest after Ange Postecoglou’s short tenure came to an end. Sean Dyche has replaced him, so could that mean Forest defenders are now worth considering?<br /><br />Make sure to give Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast a follow so you don't miss an episode. To join our Sky Sports mini league the code is 4Y5Z67<br /><br />Listen to every episode of the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast here: <a href="https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11661/13193390/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast-listen-and-subscribe-to-our-fantasy-premier-league-podcast" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast</a><br /><br />You can listen to the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast on your smart speaker by saying "ask Global Player to play Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast".<br /><br />For all the latest Premier League news, head to <a href="https://www.skysports.com/premier-league" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/premier-league</a><br /><br />To get in touch with the podcast email: fantasy@sky.uk]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[James Savundra and Mark Briggs are joined by Sam Bonfield from FPL Family for this week’s episode.<br /><br />It was a weekend of contrasting fortunes for some of the most popular forwards in FPL. Erling Haaland, Jean-Philippe Mateta and Nick Woltemade all performed well but there was disappointment for Alexander Isak, Joao Pedro and Viktor Gyokeres.<br /><br />James, Mark and Sam discuss if it’s time to get rid of those underperforming strikers or if it’s worth holding onto them a little longer.<br /><br />They also chat about Nottingham Forest after Ange Postecoglou’s short tenure came 