Cunha &amp; Mateta replacements</title><itunes:title>FPL Gameweek 28 | Best Cunha &amp; Mateta replacements</itunes:title><description><![CDATA[James Savundra and Mark Briggs are joined by European football expert Dougie Critchley for this week’s episode of the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast.<br /><br />They reflect on the big talking points from the FA Cup weekend and what impact they have in FPL. They include a red card to Wolves forward Matheus Cunha and a serious injury to Crystal Palace striker Jean-Philippe Mateta.<br /><br />They also look ahead to Gameweek 28 and discuss what you should you do with Alexander Isak and Cole Palmer. They talk captaincy too and debate whether there are any credible alternatives to Mohamed Salah this week.<br /><br />Make sure to give Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast a follow so you don't miss an episode. To join our Sky Sports mini league the code is 4Y5Z67<br /><br />Listen to every episode of the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast here: <a href="https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11661/13193390/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast-listen-and-subscribe-to-our-fantasy-premier-league-podcast" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast</a><br /><br />You can listen to the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast on your smart speaker by saying "ask Global Player to play Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast".<br /><br />For all the latest Premier League news, head to <a href="https://www.skysports.com/premier-league" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/premier-league</a><br /><br />To get in touch with the podcast email: fantasy@sky.uk]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[James Savundra and Mark Briggs are joined by European football expert Dougie Critchley for this week’s episode of the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast.<br /><br />They reflect on the big talking points from the FA Cup weekend and what impact they have in FPL. They include a red card to Wolves forward Matheus Cunha and a serious injury to Crystal Palace