/>They also look ahead to Gameweek 27. Cole Palmer is one of the most transferred out players of the week despite facing Southampton up next. Josh makes a strong case about why you should keep him.<br /><br />James, Mark and Josh also weigh up the best captaincy options. Should you stick with the reliable Mohamed Salah or risk going for someone else? Tune in to find out.<br /><br />Make sure to give Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast a follow so you don't miss an episode. To join our Sky Sports mini league the code is 4Y5Z67<br /><br />Listen to every episode of the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast here: <a href="https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11661/13193390/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast-listen-and-subscribe-to-our-fantasy-premier-league-podcast" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/sky-sports-fantasy-podcast</a><br /><br />You can listen to the Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast on your smart speaker by saying "ask Global Player to play Sky Sports Fantasy Podcast".<br /><br />For all the latest Premier League news, head to <a href="https://www.skysports.com/premier-league" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">skysports.com/premier-league</a><br /><br />To get in touch with the podcast email: fantasy@sky.uk]]></description><content:encoded><![CDATA[James Savundra and Mark Briggs are joined by former Union J band member and FPL fanatic Josh Cuthbert.<br /><br />James, Mark and Josh reflect on Gameweek 26 which was a success for those that picked Oliver Glasner as their Assistant Manager. They discuss whether chasing ‘Table Bonus’ points is the best strategy going forward.<br /><br />They also look ahead to Gameweek 27. Cole Palmer is one of the most transferred out players of the week despite facing Southampton up next. Josh makes a strong case about why you should keep him.<br /><br />James, Mark and Josh also weigh up the best captaincy options. Should you stick with the reliable Mohamed Salah or risk going for someone else? Tune in to find out.<br /><br />